const appscGroup4Lessons = {
  'g4-history': [
    ['Andhra through early and medieval history', 'The Krishna and Godavari valleys supported agriculture, internal trade and religious settlements. The Satavahanas connected parts of the Deccan through towns and trade routes, while the Ikshvakus are associated with the Buddhist monuments at Nagarjunakonda. Use coins, inscriptions and monuments together when identifying a dynasty because each source tells a different part of the story.', 'The Eastern Chalukyas ruled the Vengi region. Telugu literary history associates Nannaya with their court and his rendering of the Mahabharata. In later centuries, the Kakatiyas and Vijayanagara rulers shaped regional administration, irrigation, temple building and commerce.'],
    ['Colonial rule and the national movement', 'Colonial rule changed land revenue and trade and encouraged new networks of education, reform and print. The Indian National Congress began in 1885. The 1905 Swadeshi movement popularized boycotts and Indian enterprise, while Gandhi’s nationwide Non-Cooperation, Civil Disobedience and Quit India movements began in 1920, 1930 and 1942 respectively.', 'Study participation in Andhra alongside the national chronology. Duggirala Gopalakrishnayya is associated with the Chirala–Perala agitation, while Alluri Sitarama Raju led the Rampa rebellion of 1922–24, rooted in grievances in the forested hill areas. Compare their methods and social settings.'],
    ['State formation and cultural traditions', 'Andhra State was created in 1953 from Telugu-speaking areas of Madras State. The merger with the Telangana region of Hyderabad State formed Andhra Pradesh in 1956. The Andhra Pradesh Reorganisation Act led to the creation of Telangana in 2014. Keep those three territorial changes distinct.', 'Kuchipudi dance, Kalamkari textile traditions, Buddhist sites such as Amaravati, and Telugu literary movements illustrate different forms of regional culture. Connect each example to its place, medium and historical context.']
  ],
  'g4-polity': [
    ['Constitutional rights and duties', 'The Constitution distributes public power and protects citizens and, for some rights, all persons. Fundamental Rights in Part III include equality, freedoms and protection of life and personal liberty. Article 32 provides access to the Supreme Court for enforcement of Fundamental Rights. The Directive Principles in Part IV guide state policy, while Article 51A lists Fundamental Duties.'],
    ['Representative institutions', 'Parliament consists of the President and two Houses. In the parliamentary system, the Council of Ministers headed by the Prime Minister is collectively responsible to the Lok Sabha. States have a Governor, a Council of Ministers headed by the Chief Minister and a legislature. The judiciary interprets laws and reviews whether public action is consistent with the Constitution.'],
    ['Local administration', 'The 73rd and 74th constitutional amendments provide the framework for rural and urban local government respectively. A Gram Sabha is the body of registered voters in the village area, while a Gram Panchayat is an elected institution. A municipality performs local civic functions in an urban area. State and district officials carry out administrative and statutory duties, while elected local bodies represent local priorities and exercise powers entrusted to them under state law.']
  ],
  'g4-geography': [
    ['Landforms and water', 'India’s major physical regions include the Himalayas, northern plains, peninsular plateau, coastal plains and islands. Andhra Pradesh includes an Eastern Ghats belt, coastal plains and interior plateau areas. The Krishna and Godavari flow east to the Bay of Bengal, and their delta deposits form productive alluvial tracts. Rainfall, drainage and access to irrigation differ between coastal and inland districts.'],
    ['Resources, crops and industry', 'A resource is valuable when it can be used with available technology and institutions. Delta irrigation supports paddy cultivation, while rain-fed areas often rely on crops adaptable to less dependable rainfall. Mineral supply, power, skilled labour, markets and transport influence industrial location. A coastal port, for example, can lower freight costs for industries that move large quantities of raw materials.'],
    ['Population and settlement', 'Population density is population divided by land area. Settlement patterns depend on water, employment, transport, terrain and public services. Urbanization measures the share of people living in urban areas, and migration can reshape population distribution without changing the country’s total population. In map questions, identify the physical feature first and then explain how it affects a livelihood or settlement.']
  ],
  'g4-economy': [
    ['Output, sectors and development', 'GDP measures the value of final production within a country over a period. GSDP is the corresponding state-level measure. Constant-price figures help separate changes in output from price changes. The primary sector obtains raw materials, the secondary sector processes or constructs, and the tertiary sector supplies services. Growth describes rising output, while development also considers health, education and access to opportunity.'],
    ['Andhra Pradesh economy', 'Agriculture and aquaculture draw on coastal and delta resources, while industry and services depend on factors such as transport, urban markets and the workforce. Different regions face different constraints, including irrigation reliability or access to infrastructure. To read a state budget, distinguish receipts from spending and current expenditure from investment in assets. To compare sectors, check the year, units and price basis of the numbers.'],
    ['Public schemes and social issues', 'A public scheme can address a specific barrier such as lack of income, unaffordable health services or limited access to education. Examine the target group, delivery method and outcome. The amount spent is an input. The number of people reached is an output. Improvement in learning, health or incomes is an outcome. Check the current official notification for eligibility and benefits.']
  ],
  'g4-science': [
    ['Physics and chemistry in daily life', 'A circuit needs a complete conducting path for current to flow. In household circuits, parallel connections allow devices to operate independently. Acids and bases can be distinguished using suitable indicators. At about 25°C, pH 7 is neutral and smaller values are more acidic. Heat travels through solids by conduction, through moving fluids by convection and through electromagnetic waves by radiation.'],
    ['Biology and public health', 'Cells carry out the basic processes of living organisms. Plants use light energy to make sugars from water and carbon dioxide during photosynthesis. In humans, digestion breaks down food into absorbable components, and the circulatory system transports many of those components to tissues. In public health, distinguish prevention, detection and treatment. Safe water and sanitation reduce exposure to many causes of disease.'],
    ['Information technology', 'Hardware refers to physical components, while software is the set of instructions they execute. An operating system manages memory, files and devices and runs applications. A web browser retrieves web pages, while a search engine indexes pages to help locate information. For office records, sound practice includes checking source reliability, restricting access to sensitive files and maintaining backups.']
  ],
  'g4-environment': [
    ['Ecosystems and environmental pressures', 'Living organisms and their surroundings form an ecosystem. Producers convert energy into organic matter, consumers obtain energy by feeding, and decomposers recycle nutrients. Habitat loss, pollution and invasive species can reduce biodiversity. Air and water pollution refer to harmful substances in those media, while climate change describes long-term shifts in climate patterns that can amplify other pressures.'],
    ['Risk and disasters in Andhra Pradesh', 'A hazard can cause harm, but risk also depends on who and what is exposed and how vulnerable they are. A cyclone of similar intensity can have very different impacts in two places because of settlement patterns, buildings, warning systems and access to shelters. Coastal Andhra is exposed to cyclones, storm surges and flooding. Drought and heat also matter for livelihoods and public services.'],
    ['The disaster management cycle', 'Mitigation reduces future harm through measures such as safer siting and resilient infrastructure. Preparedness includes planning, training and warning arrangements. Response addresses immediate needs after a threat or event, while recovery restores services and livelihoods. In an exam answer, pair each phase with a practical local example and distinguish warnings issued by expert agencies from field action by local authorities.']
  ],
  'g4-current': [
    ['What to study', 'Track Andhra Pradesh, national and international developments relevant to governance, economics, society, environment and science. For each item, capture its date, location, responsible institution and relevance to the syllabus. Keep the event itself separate from background concepts, such as a budget announcement from how government accounts are classified.'],
    ['How to verify an item', 'Begin with the issuing body or its published decision. A proposal, announcement, notification, commencement date and implementation report can refer to different stages of the same measure. Keep the reference period with any statistic. A provisional estimate can change in a later publication. Compare claims made about different years only when their definitions and units are compatible.'],
    ['Build a revisable notebook', 'Use a one-page weekly log organized by subject. Write a factual question such as “Which institution issued the notice?” and a conceptual one such as “Which problem does the measure address?” Work backward from the topic list and refresh recent examples before the exam. Store the original source link alongside each answer.']
  ],
  'g4-numeracy': [
    ['Numbers and simplification', 'Use brackets first, then powers, multiplication and division from left to right, and addition and subtraction from left to right. Convert fractions to a common denominator before adding. For example, 3/4 + 5/6 = 9/12 + 10/12 = 19/12. Estimate roughly before calculating to catch misplaced signs and decimal points.'],
    ['Percentages and averages', 'A percentage is a fraction out of 100. If a value rises from 80 to 100, the rise is 20 out of the original 80, or 25%. Returning from 100 to 80 is a 20% fall because the base altered. The arithmetic mean is total divided by count, so the mean of 8, 12, 15 and 21 is 56 ÷ 4 = 14. For a combined average, use the sizes of the groups as weights.'],
    ['Ratios and proportions', 'A ratio compares quantities in the same units. If 64 objects are divided in the ratio 3:5, each of the eight parts contains 8 objects, yielding 24 and 40. In direct proportion, one quantity grows by the same factor as the other. In inverse proportion, one rises while the other falls in such a way that their product stays fixed, as with equal-rate workers and time for a fixed job.']
  ],
  'g4-applied-arithmetic': [
    ['Profit, loss and interest', 'Profit equals selling price minus cost price. Divide that difference by the cost price to get the profit rate. Selling a ₹500 item for ₹575 gives a ₹75 profit, or 15%. A discount applies to the marked price. Simple interest is principal × annual rate × time when the rate is written as a decimal and the time in years. Compound interest uses the updated balance in each period.'],
    ['Time, work, speed and distance', 'Represent work as a rate. If two people finish the same job in 6 and 3 hours individually, their rates are 1/6 and 1/3 of the job per hour. Together they finish it in 2 hours when both rates remain constant. Speed = distance ÷ time. For different speeds across a trip, divide total distance by total time. Convert units before using a formula, for example 72 km/h = 20 m/s.'],
    ['Mensuration', 'Perimeter measures distance around a shape, area measures its surface and volume measures the space inside a solid. A 12 m by 5 m rectangle has perimeter 34 m and area 60 m². A cuboid with those base dimensions and height 2 m has volume 120 m³. Use consistent length units before squaring or cubing.']
  ],
  'g4-reasoning': [
    ['Relationships, classes and ordering', 'An analogy matches a relationship, such as seed-to-plant and egg-to-bird, both starting forms and developed organisms. Classification asks for a common property or the exception. In ordering problems, write each clue as a relation and build a line or table. Two partial orders may yield several possible arrangements, so infer only what all valid arrangements share.'],
    ['Series, codes and directions', 'For number series, test differences, ratios and alternating patterns. The differences in 4, 9, 16, 25 are 5, 7 and 9, suggesting a next term of 36. For letter codes, number the alphabet and apply the rule to each letter before checking the options. For directions, draw a compass and track each turn and distance in order, paying attention to the person’s current facing direction.'],
    ['Tables and charts', 'Check the title, unit, time period and denominator first. A bar chart commonly compares categories, while a line graph can show a sequence over time. Use addition for totals and division for rates or shares. An increase from 50% to 60% is 10 percentage points, or a 20% rise relative to the starting percentage. Watch for totals repeated in table rows.']
  ],
  'g4-en-grammar': [
    ['Parts of speech and sentence formation', 'Nouns name things and ideas, pronouns stand in for nouns or noun phrases, and verbs express actions or states. Adjectives describe nouns, and adverbs can modify verbs, adjectives or other adverbs. In “The clerk carefully checked the file,” clerk is a noun, checked a verb and carefully an adverb. Find the subject and finite verb before analysing modifiers.'],
    ['Tense, agreement, articles and prepositions', 'Choose tense from the time relationship. “The clerk sent the report yesterday” uses the simple past for a completed action with a stated past time. In “The list of candidates is on the desk,” the head noun list is singular. Use a or an before an indefinite singular noun based on sound, as in “an hour” and “a university.” Use the when the intended reference is identifiable. Study conventional prepositions such as “interested in” and “responsible for.”'],
    ['Error spotting and blanks', 'After identifying the main subject and verb, check tense markers, pronoun reference, parallel structure and word choice. In “Each of the reports are ready,” replace are with is because each is singular. For a blank, read the full sentence to determine whether it needs a noun, verb or connector, then reread your choice in context.']
  ],
  'g4-en-vocab': [
    ['Meaning and register', 'Synonyms have similar meanings, but their tone and use can differ. Concise and brief can both describe short writing, while concise suggests efficiently expressed ideas. Antonyms express an opposite meaning in a given sense, such as expand and contract. In a one-word substitution, replace a description precisely. Someone who cannot read or write is illiterate.'],
    ['Idioms and spelling', 'An idiom has a conventional meaning that cannot always be obtained by adding the literal meanings of its words. “At short notice” means with little warning. Learn spelling in word families where useful, but note changes such as receive and reception. Review commonly confused pairs in sentences, for example affect as a verb and effect as a noun in their most common uses.'],
    ['Reading comprehension', 'Read for the passage’s main point and notice how supporting sentences illustrate, qualify or challenge it. Detail questions require locating the relevant evidence. Inference questions require a conclusion supported by the text. For vocabulary in context, substitute a proposed meaning and reread the sentence. For tone, distinguish the writer’s attitude from the subject of the passage.']
  ],
  'g4-te-grammar': [
    ['Grammar and correct usage', 'In తెలుగు grammar, identify the subject, its role and the verb ending before correcting a sentence. In “రాము పుస్తకం చదివాడు”, రాము is the doer, పుస్తకం is the object and చదివాడు is the past-tense verb. Compare “రాము చదివాడు” with “సీత చదివింది” to see the effect of the subject on the verb form.'],
    ['Vocabulary relationships', 'పర్యాయపదాలు are words with similar meanings, for example నీరు and జలం. A pair can differ in formality, so consider the sentence before substituting one word for another. వ్యతిరేక పదాలు express an opposite meaning, for example లాభం and నష్టం. Create one example sentence for each word so that you can distinguish meaning from usage.'],
    ['Sandhi and samasam', 'సంధి concerns the change at the boundary when sounds combine. In దేవ + ఆలయం → దేవాలయం, the vowels join under a sandhi rule. సమాసం concerns the grammatical relationship between words joined into a compound. రామబాణం can be expanded as రాముని బాణం, where the relation is possession. In an exam, identify the joined forms and show the expansion or sound change requested.']
  ],
  'g4-te-writing': [
    ['Comprehension in Telugu', 'Read the passage once for the theme, then identify the sentence that supports each answer. Notice connectors such as కానీ, అయితే and అందువల్ల because they mark contrast, conditions or consequences depending on context. To summarize a paragraph, state its central idea in your own words and keep only the details that explain it.'],
    ['Correction and idioms', 'In a correction exercise, check spelling, agreement and the sequence of ideas before changing vocabulary. “వాళ్లు వచ్చాడు” can be corrected to “వాళ్లు వచ్చారు” for plural agreement. Interpret expressions as units. “చేతులు దులుపుకోవడం” can mean distancing oneself from responsibility, so context determines whether the phrase is literal or idiomatic.'],
    ['Short and functional writing', 'Identify purpose, audience and format before writing. A brief official request should state the subject, give the relevant facts in order and end with the requested action. A short descriptive paragraph needs one central point and supporting details. Reread the final text for punctuation, repeated wording and appropriate formality.']
  ],
  'g4-computer-basics': [
    ['Hardware and operating systems', 'The processor executes instructions, memory holds active programs and data, and storage keeps files when power is off. Common peripherals include keyboards, scanners and printers. The operating system provides a file system and manages devices, running processes and user permissions. An application is software designed for a user task, such as editing a document.'],
    ['Files and folders', 'A file stores information, while a folder organizes files and other folders. A path identifies a location. A file extension often indicates its format, such as .pdf or .xlsx. Renaming an extension alone generally does not convert a file to the new format. Copying leaves the original in place, while moving relocates it. For office work, consistent names help distinguish drafts from signed or final versions.'],
    ['Security and reliability', 'Use strong unique passwords and multifactor authentication where offered, install authorized updates and keep copies of important records. Be wary of messages that create urgency, request credentials or use unexpected attachments. Verify the sender through a separate trusted channel, and restrict access to sensitive documents to the people who need it.']
  ],
  'g4-office-tools': [
    ['Word processing and presentations', 'Use styles for headings to keep documents consistent, and use margins, page breaks and print preview to control the page layout. Tables are useful when row and column relationships matter. A presentation should be readable from a distance. Give each slide a clear point, use charts for comparisons, and keep supporting detail in speaker notes when appropriate.'],
    ['Spreadsheet calculations', 'A cell reference combines a column letter and row number, for example B2. A formula begins with an equals sign. SUM(B2:B6) totals the five cells in that range. A copied relative reference adjusts with position, while $B$2 stays fixed when copied. Sort or filter the complete data range so that values stay attached to the correct records. Use numeric date and number formats for reliable calculations.'],
    ['Internet and email', 'A browser opens web pages and can submit forms or download files. Verify that the address and domain match the intended public office. Email To identifies the main recipients, CC copies visible recipients and BCC hides that recipient from other recipients. An official message needs a useful subject, a concise request and the correct document attached or linked with appropriate access.']
  ],
  'g4-office-practice': [
    ['Typing and proofreading', 'Practise touch typing through short accuracy-focused sessions, then introduce time limits. Track both speed and mistakes because a fast copy can still be unusable if names, dates or figures are wrong. Compare the completed text with the original in short blocks, checking punctuation and line breaks as well as words. Where the notice specifies Telugu typing, practise the required input method and layout.'],
    ['Clerical workflow', 'A typical workflow receives a document, records its reference and date, directs it to the appropriate person, drafts or enters information, checks it, and files or dispatches the result. Write status and next action in a tracking register. Use the same unique reference in the register and correspondence. Separate draft files from final versions and protect personal information.'],
    ['Practice exercise', 'Take a fictional request for a certificate. Create an entry in a spreadsheet with reference, received date, applicant, subject and status. Draft a short acknowledgement in a word processor, save the final version and check names and dates against the entry. Repeat under a timer to practise the specific typing, spreadsheet and document tasks named in your recruitment notice.']
  ]
};
